\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I lift my heart to Thee,
\par Saviour divine;
\par For Thou art all to me,
\par And I am Thine.
\par Is there on earth a closer  bond than this:
\par That my Beloved's mine, and I amHis?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thine am I by all ties;
\par But chiefly Thine,
\par That through Thy sacrifice
\par Thou, Lord, art mine.
\par By Thine own cords of love, sosweeter wound
\par Around me, I to Thee am closely bound.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. To Thee, Thou dying Lamb,
\par I all things owe;
\par All that I have, and am,
\par And all I know.
\par All that I have is now no longer mine,
\par And I am not my own; Lord, I am Thine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\b0 
\par \ulnone 4. How can I, Lord, withhold
\par Life's brightest hour
\par From Thee; or gathered gold,
\par Or any power?
\par Why should I keep one precious thing from Thee,
\par When Thou hast given Thine own dear self for me?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. I pray Thee, Saviour, keep
\par Me in Thy love,
\par Until death's holy sleep
\par Shall me remove
\par To that fair realm where, sin andsorrow o'er,
\par Thou and Thine own are one forevermore.
\par                                           Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
